                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Super Hyperactive Ninja[/h1]\n\nNinjas and coffee? Maybe it isn't historically accurate, but it sure as heck makes sense. Ninjas are always flipping out and stuff, and they don't seem to ever slow down.\n\nIf the cut-scenes are any indication [i]Super Hyperactive Ninja[/i] draws a large part of its inspiration from the iconic [i]Megaman[/i] series at least in its story and presentation, with a story centered in the year \"15XX\" and a nostalgic opening that should be familiar to any fans of the Blue Bomber. The retro similarities end there though, as [i]Hyperactive Ninja[/i] has an entirely unique and hectic mechanic that makes it a fresh and modern platforming experience.\n\n[h1]Gameplay[/h1]\n\n[i]Super Hyperactive Ninja[/i] is all about going fast, it's all about taking a chug of that sweet caffeine and charging through a maze of obstacles at break-neck speed. It's not as simple as just running through, however. You'll need the coffee to get yourself amped up first, and plenty of armed Shogun baddies will be blocking your path so plan your caffeine/fuel usage accordingly. This is a fast game, so fast that you won't get a chance to stop and breathe while utilizing your hyperactive mode to push past the guards in your way so be ready to think quick and react with your thumbs even quicker!\n\nThere's a certain art and a certain pattern to breaking through each stage though, and enemies can only be defeated if approached from the back. Finding the right route with enemies that can be dispatched is the key here, and making a sudden bad decision in your caffeine-fueled frenzy can lead you right into the blade of a forward-facing Shogun. Keeping a constant and steady pace in later levels is going to require a careful planning of paths to charge your way through, and that sort of crazy split-second decision making is where all the fun is.\n\n[h1]Final Thought[/h1]\n\nEveryone from casual action game fans to pure platformer junkies should take note, [i]Hyperactive Ninja[/i] is a quick shot of adrenaline pumping speed running action that charges full-speed ahead from start to finish. Ironically enough, this is the perfect coffee-break speed-running arcade game to get your caffeine-buzz going in-between bigger gaming sessions or important tasks.\n\n[i]This review made possible through the consideration and contribution of [url=http://store.steampowered.com/curator/24117656-IndiePromo/]IndiePromo[/url] and the developer/publisher. \n\nEmail contact@dnbmedia.co for requests & game promotions\n[/i]",
